<!--
  Shared head assets for every marketing subpage (features/*, for/*,
  compare). The homepage (index.stx) predates this partial and keeps its
  own inline copy of the same design system. Tokens here are copied from
  it verbatim and must stay in sync if the brand ever changes. Subpages
  include this once instead of carrying 1,300 duplicated CSS lines each.

  Expects the including page to define appName in its server script.
  NOTE: never write a literal script tag inside these comments. The stx
  processor scans for script blocks before comment semantics apply, and
  it will eat the comment closer, turning the rest of the page into one
  giant HTML comment (that bug shipped once already).

  The theme pre-paint script sits AFTER the font links on purpose: a
  script block at the very top of a partial is treated as the partial's
  component script and stripped from the output.
-->
{{-- Favicons, font preconnects and the font stylesheet moved to
     config/ui.ts app.head (stx-standards 04-head): injected into full
     documents via injectConfigHeadTags (href-deduped) and into fragments
     via the document shell, so pages including this partial must not
     re-add them. --}}
{{-- No <style> block: rule 3 / §11.1. This partial's 219 rules are
     config/crosswind.ts's `marketingCss()` preflight, wrapped once in the two
     layout groups that include it -- `home` for index.stx, which includes this
     directly, and `marketing` for layouts/marketing.stx, which every feature,
     comparison and docs page extends. The scope matters: a preflight reaches
     every page, and forty class names in this app mean different things on
     different surfaces. The design tokens went to `paletteCss()`. --}}
{{-- Scripts sit AFTER the style block on purpose: a script as the
     partial's FIRST element is treated as its component script and
     stripped from the output (the deleted font links used to shield
     them; the style block shields them now). --}}
{{-- The pre-paint theme script is app.colorMode in config/ui.ts now. --}}
